{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You have brought upon him a great sin.</b> For they rejoiced in the corruption through dancing because you proclaimed a festival for them for the morrow — and this is worse than the rebellion and treason they committed with the calf, and for this greater mercy was sought, as he said: אַתֶּם חֲטָאתֶם חֲטָאָה גְדוֹלָה, and likewise in his prayer he said: אָנָּא חָטָא הָעָם הַזֶּה חֲטָאָה גְדוֹלָה, and likewise in the order of the thirteen attributes he mentioned עָוֹן וָפֶשַׁע וְחַטָּאָה (Exodus 34:7), and likewise in his prayer there: וְסָלַחְתָּ לַעֲוֹנֵנוּ וּלְחַטָּאתֵנוּ (Exodus 34:9). And therefore he said: even though they gathered against you to compel you to make the calf for them — what did they do to you that you were required to proclaim a festival for them for the morrow? For this was the cause of the dancing they did for the calf's celebration, which was worse than its making."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:47.851800293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}